Description: An automated method to quantitatively identify and extract age plateaus
    from LA-ICP-MS depth profiling data of zircon U-Pb geochronology. The package
    implements ARIMA-based outlier detection, LOESS smoothing, PELT changepoint
    segmentation, multi-step plateau filtering (forward/reverse), optional Bayesian
    MCMC posterior analysis, and publication-ready visualization. Supports four
    input formats: direct U-Pb ages (Age68/Age75/Age76), raw isotope counts
    (Pb206/Pb207/U238), isotopic ratios (Pb206_U238/Pb207_U235/Pb207_Pb206), or
    ages carrying a per-point 1-sigma (Age68 plus Age68_1s). The latter switches
    the plateau age to an inverse-variance weighted mean and reports MSWD, so a
    plateau can be tested for internal consistency rather than only for
    precision. All core functionality runs on base R alone - OOXML
    reading/writing, U-Pb age conversion, PELT segmentation, ARIMA order
    selection and plotting are implemented inside the package, so results do not
    depend on the changing behaviour of third-party packages.
    v1.2.0 adds a full uncertainty budget (random vs systematic, including the
    decay-constant contribution), a parameter-sensitivity sweep, a monotonic-
    subsequence plateau selector that no longer collapses to two plateaus on
    noisy data, input validation, and an optional robust-LOESS pre-processing
    path that removes the need for ARIMA outlier screening.
    v1.3.0 adds the per-point-uncertainty input format and MSWD, a smooth =
    "none" switch for input that already carries a down-hole fractionation
    correction, and processing of sheets that stack several zircons.
    Method described in Wang et al. (2026), JGR: Solid Earth, 131, e2025JB033324.
